Jukka Lahtinen wrote:
> ShuJaWa <jashya@gmail.com> writes:
>
>> just got started on nethack, but can't seem to get further than the
>> 5th or 6th level. anybody got tips? :D

Tip not about the game - On UseNet please go ahead and spell out your
words.  Abbreviated words tend to show you're a newbie to newsgroups as
well as to Nethack.  UseNet has a different culture than other on-line
systems and there are many reasons for that fact.

> Tips depend on what most often kills you.
> Consider every death a lesson and try to learn something about it.

Think both tactics and strategy.  Tactics is the nearby situation that
managed to kill you.  Strategy is what you did a few levels ago that set
up the context that managed to kill you.  Have bad strategy and no
amount of tactical skill will help.

> Don't get surrounded by hostile monsters. Try to have an escape route
> clear, and fight your fights in corridors instead of rooms, whenever you
> see more than one hostile creature. 

Run to the upstairs to heal.  That level is explored and cleared.

Hunger can drive you down so develop an eating strategy.  If you are
leaving behind the bodies of nutritious monsters you may be rushing down
fast enough to get yourself killed.

Use your quiver and use more missile combat.  Few monsters carry enough
missiles to do you much damage but you can gather enough missiles so a
lot of monsters are dead before they get to to.  Even extremely powerful
monsters are easier to kill when they do reach melee range if they've
been peppered with daggers or arrows or rocks as they advanced towards
you.

To me the biggest tip for a newbie - Understand that for many it takes
years to ascend.  The learning curve of Nethack is so much longer
compared to other computer games that it seems flat.  On the one hand
that makes Nethack frustrating to play.  On the other hand that makes
Nethack still interesting to play many years later.


